{#
  The playground hub — the de-versioned home page (the plan's own
  disposition for /v6/unified-guidance: "keep as-is, becomes / (home)";
  here that's /playground/hub, since the site's actual "/" still serves
  the frozen versions index — see the playground build's own decisions
  log for why). The hero is carried over unchanged from /v6/unified-guidance.

  Navigation (see page.notes.md): the side navigation (layouts/main.html,
  partials/side-nav.njk) replaced the context pane. Its lists are filters of
  this one all-guidance list — ?list= and ?case= (view-model.js). Pinned
  guides carry a star, can be
  pinned from each row, and sit first whenever nothing narrows the list.

  Layout: the green hero now sits at the top of the main column, beside the
  nav, rather than full-bleed across the page (_app-side-nav.scss rounds
  it), so the nav starts under the Defra header on every page.

  Filters (.app-filter, _app-filter.scss) are a horizontal row inside
  the main column, above the results list — a hand-ported
  adaptation of the MoJ Design System's Filter component (header /
  selected-filters-with-removable-tags / options), not the installed
  package, laid out horizontally since MoJ's own docs only cover a
  vertical filter pane. Every field in .app-filter__options is always
  visible, in-flow, with no collapse/disclosure/overlay behaviour — GDS
  doesn't sanction modal-style dropdown panels, so this deliberately
  isn't the popover-per-facet treatment an earlier pass of this page
  tried. There's no govuk-grid-row split any more: with the sidebar
  column gone, both the filter row and the results list are plain
  full-width siblings in the main column. See
  page.notes.md for the full reasoning, including why Category/Scheme/
  Year moved off plain <select> (each progressively enhanced with
  accessible-autocomplete, since the real service expects many options
  per facet) while State (a fixed, three-value enum) stays checkboxes
  and Sort-by stays a plain select.

  Filtering/sorting/search is a real GET round-trip (view-model.js reads
  category/scheme/year/state/sort/q straight off req.query and filters
  buildManageGuidanceSearchResults() server-side), not client-side JS —
  the retired hub/search/page.njk this was ported from filtered entirely
  client-side against an embedded resultsJson, which meant none of it
  worked with JavaScript off; see page.notes.md for why that changed.
  #hub-filters is one real <form> covering Category/Scheme/Year/State (a
  hidden q field mirrors the current search so applying a filter doesn't
  drop it); Sort by sits outside that form in the results header but
  submits with it via its own form="hub-filters" attribute. Selected
  filters render as plain <a> tags (remove one filter = follow a link with
  that param dropped, per selectedFilters/buildHref in view-model.js), and
  Clear filters is a plain link to the bare page — no JS needed for any of
  that. pageScripts below is now pure progressive enhancement only:
  accessible-autocomplete on Category/Scheme/Year, and an optional
  auto-submit-on-change for Sort by.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/base.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/input/macro.njk" import govukInput %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/checkboxes/macro.njk" import govukCheckboxes %}
{% from "govuk/components/select/macro.njk" import govukSelect %}
{% from "govuk/components/tag/macro.njk" import govukTag %}
{% from "partials/side-nav-icon.njk" import sideNavIcon %}

{% set pageName = "RPA Guidance hub" %}

{% set stateTags = {
  "Draft": { text: "Draft", classes: "govuk-tag--grey" },
  "Awaiting review": { text: "Awaiting review", classes: "govuk-tag--yellow" },
  "Live": { text: "Live", classes: "govuk-tag--turquoise" }
} %}


{% block content %}

  <div class="defra-home-header">
    <div class="govuk-width-container govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
      <h1 class="defra-home-header__title">RPA Guidance hub</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="govuk-width-container">
      <form class="defra-home-header__search" method="get" action="/playground/hub" role="search">
        <label class="govuk-visually-hidden" for="defra-home-header-search-input">Search all guidance</label>
        <div class="defra-search-bar defra-search-bar--with-kbd">
          <input class="govuk-input defra-search-bar__input" id="defra-home-header-search-input" name="q" type="search" autocomplete="off" data-page-search placeholder="Search all guidance, or paste an error message or scheme code" value="{{ initialSearchQuery }}">
          <kbd class="app-search-kbd" data-page-search-kbd hidden></kbd>
          <button class="defra-search-bar__button defra-search-bar__button--on-green" type="submit">
            <span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Search</span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="27" height="27" viewBox="0 0 27 27" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="12.0161" cy="11.0161" r="8.51613" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" fill="none"></circle><line x1="17.8668" y1="17.3587" x2="26.4475" y2="25.9393" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"></line></svg>
          </button>
        </div>
        {# What the hub covers, until a search starts and says so instead. #}
        <p class="defra-home-header__description govuk-!-margin-top-2 govuk-!-margin-bottom-0" role="status" data-search-status>Currently covers Countryside Stewardship Final Payments</p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>

{#
  A question (query-kind.js) gets the guides API's AI search of every indexed
  guide (partials/search-results.njk); other words are counted in every API
  guide (partials/keyword-results.njk). The guide list below still filters on
  the same words, as a mock.
#}
{% if aiSearch %}
  {% include "playground/hub/partials/search-results.njk" %}
{% elif keywordSearch %}
  {% include "playground/hub/partials/keyword-results.njk" %}
{% endif %}

<div class="app-hub-columns">

  {#
    Filter results floats beside the guides as a guide's contents list does
    beside its text (_app-guide.scss): stuck in view as the list scrolls,
    and scrolling itself if taller than the window. One real GET form, so
    a no-JS visit still filters; Sort by submits with it (form="hub-filters").
    The counts are made up for now.
  #}
  <aside class="app-hub-filters" aria-labelledby="hub-filters-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m app-hub-filters__title" id="hub-filters-heading">Filter results</h2>

    {% if selectedFilters.length %}
      <div class="app-filter__selected app-hub-filters__selected">
        <h3 class="govuk-visually-hidden">Selected filters</h3>
        <ul class="app-filter__tags">
          {% for filter in selectedFilters %}
            <li>
              <a class="app-filter__tag" href="{{ filter.href }}">
                <span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Remove filter</span>
                {{ filter.label }}
                <span class="app-filter__tag-remove" aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
        <a class="govuk-link app-hub-filters__clear" href="{{ clearFiltersHref }}">Clear filters</a>
      </div>
    {% endif %}

    <form id="hub-filters" method="get" action="/playground/hub#guide-results">
      <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{ initialSearchQuery }}">
      {% if selectedList %}<input type="hidden" name="list" value="{{ selectedList }}">{% endif %}
      {% if selectedBookmark %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ selectedBookmark.param }}" value="{{ selectedBookmark.ref }}">{% endif %}

      {{ govukCheckboxes({
        idPrefix: "audience",
        name: "audience",
        classes: "govuk-checkboxes--small",
        formGroup: { classes: "app-hub-filters__group" },
        fieldset: { legend: { text: "Who it's for", classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--s" } },
        items: audienceItems
      }) }}

      {{ govukCheckboxes({
        idPrefix: "system",
        name: "system",
        classes: "govuk-checkboxes--small",
        formGroup: { classes: "app-hub-filters__group" },
        fieldset: { legend: { text: "System used", classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--s" } },
        items: systemItems
      }) }}

      {{ govukCheckboxes({
        idPrefix: "year",
        name: "year",
        classes: "govuk-checkboxes--small",
        formGroup: { classes: "app-hub-filters__group" },
        fieldset: { legend: { text: "Scheme year", classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--s" } },
        items: yearItems
      }) }}

      {% if isDesigner %}
        {{ govukCheckboxes({
          idPrefix: "state",
          name: "state",
          classes: "govuk-checkboxes--small",
          formGroup: { classes: "app-hub-filters__group" },
          fieldset: { legend: { text: "State", classes: "govuk-fieldset__legend--s" } },
          items: [
            { value: "draft", text: "Draft", checked: stateChecked.draft },
            { value: "awaiting-review", text: "Awaiting review", checked: stateChecked["awaiting-review"] },
            { value: "live", text: "Live", checked: stateChecked.live }
          ]
        }) }}
      {% endif %}

      <div class="app-hub-filters__group">
        <h3 class="govuk-heading-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">Scheme</h3>
        <p class="govuk-hint govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">Hidden while every guide is CS. Appears when a second scheme is added.</p>
      </div>

      {{ govukButton({
        text: "Apply filters",
        classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-0"
      }) }}
    </form>
  </aside>

  <div class="app-hub-results">
    <div class="app-hub-results__header" id="guide-results">
      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l govuk-!-margin-bottom-1">{{ results.length }} guide{{ "s" if results.length != 1 }}</h2>
      {% if results.length %}
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-1 app-hub-results__showing">Showing 1 to {{ results.length }}</p>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="app-hub-results__sort">
        <label class="govuk-label app-hub-results__sort-label" for="sort">Sort by:</label>
        {{ govukSelect({
          id: "sort",
          name: "sort",
          classes: "app-hub-results__sort-select",
          formGroup: { classes: "govuk-!-margin-bottom-0" },
          attributes: { form: "hub-filters", "data-sort-select": true },
          items: [
            { value: "updated-newest", text: "Recently updated", selected: selectedSort == "updated-newest" },
            { value: "updated-oldest", text: "Oldest updated", selected: selectedSort == "updated-oldest" },
            { value: "most-relevant", text: "Most relevant", selected: selectedSort == "most-relevant" }
          ]
        }) }}
        {% if not initialSearchQuery %}
          <span class="app-hub-results__sort-hint">(Most relevant once you search)</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>

    {% if results.length == 0 %}
      <p class="govuk-body">No guides match your search or filters. Try removing some filters or using different search terms.</p>
    {% else %}
      <ul class="app-search-results">
        {% for result in results %}
          <li class="app-search-results__item{% if result.pinned %} app-search-results__item--pinned{% endif %}" id="result-{{ result.id }}">

            <div class="app-search-results__top">
              <div class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
                {% if result.versionTag %}{{ govukTag(result.versionTag) }}{% endif %}
                {% for state in result.states %}{{ govukTag(stateTags[state]) }} {% endfor %}
                {% if result.pinned %}<strong class="govuk-tag govuk-tag--grey app-search-results__pinned-tag">Pinned</strong>{% endif %}
              </div>
              <form class="app-pin-toggle" method="post" action="{{ pinToggleHref }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="documentId" value="{{ result.id }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="returnTo" value="{{ currentHref }}">
                <input type="hidden" name="anchor" value="pin-{{ result.id }}">
                <button type="submit" class="app-pin-toggle__button" id="pin-{{ result.id }}" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if result.pinned else 'false' }}" data-pin-toggle>
                  {{ sideNavIcon("star-filled" if result.pinned else "star") }}
                  <span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Pin {{ result.title }}</span>
                </button>
              </form>
            </div>

            <h3 class="govuk-heading-s app-search-results__name">
              <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ result.overviewHref }}?from=search&q={{ initialSearchQuery | urlencode }}">{{ result.title }}</a>
            </h3>

            {% if result.resumeLabel %}
              <p class="govuk-body-s app-search-results__resume">Continue from <strong>{{ result.resumeLabel }}</strong></p>
            {% endif %}

            <p class="govuk-body app-search-results__description">{{ result.description }}</p>

            <p class="govuk-body-s app-search-results__dates">Last updated: {{ result.lastUpdated }} &middot; Published: {{ result.published }}</p>

          </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

</div>

{% endblock %}

{% block pageScripts %}
  {# accessible-autocomplete is loaded by layouts/main.html on side-nav pages. #}
  <script src="/public/javascripts/query-kind.js"></script>
  <script>
    (function () {
      // Filtering itself is a real GET round-trip now (view-model.js), not
      // client-side JS, so it works with JavaScript off. Everything left
      // here is pure progressive enhancement on top of controls that
      // already work without it.

      // Sort by already submits with the rest of #hub-filters (via its own
      // form="hub-filters" attribute — see page.njk) once Apply filters is
      // pressed; auto-submitting on change as well just saves that extra
      // click, entirely optional since the fallback (change it, then press
      // Apply) already works with JS off.
      // After pinning/unpinning, pin-toggle redirects back to #pin-<id> —
      // the star button itself, so a keyboard user keeps their place.
      if (window.location.hash.indexOf('#pin-') === 0) {
        var star = document.getElementById(window.location.hash.slice(1))
        if (star) star.focus()
      }

      // Ctrl K (Cmd K on a Mac) searches all guidance everywhere: here it
      // comes to this box (side-nav.js), and the box says so. Ctrl F is left
      // to the browser: it searches a guide only on a guide's page.
      var searchInput = document.getElementById('defra-home-header-search-input')
      var searchKbd = document.querySelector('[data-page-search-kbd]')
      if (searchInput && searchKbd) {
        var isMac = /Mac|iPhone|iPad/.test(navigator.platform)
        searchKbd.textContent = isMac ? '\u2318 K' : 'Ctrl K'
        searchKbd.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true')
        searchKbd.hidden = false
        searchInput.setAttribute('aria-keyshortcuts', isMac ? 'Meta+K' : 'Control+K')
      }

      // A search replaces what the hub covers with what it's doing. An AI
      // search reads every guide, so its next page takes a while.
      var searchStatus = document.querySelector('[data-search-status]')
      if (searchInput && searchStatus) {
        searchInput.form.addEventListener('submit', function () {
          if (!searchInput.value.trim()) return
          searchStatus.textContent = window.appQueryKind.isQuestion(searchInput.value)
            ? 'Searching all guidance. This can take up to a minute.'
            : 'Searching all guidance.'
        })
      }

      var sortSelect = document.querySelector('[data-sort-select]')
      if (sortSelect) {
        sortSelect.addEventListener('change', function () {
          sortSelect.form.submit()
        })
      }
    })()
  </script>
{% endblock %}
